B-band would make it unique so far. We present further evidence for its Galactic nature from imaging under excellent seeing conditions (0.3-0.6 arcsec). This dust cloud could be the first optically identified counterpart of a new type of molecular cloud recently discovered by Heithausen (2004).","abstract_source_suggest":{"input":"arXiv"}}],"primary_arxiv_category":["astro-ph"],"titles":[{"title":"A Tiny galactic dust cloud projected onto NGC 3269?"},{"source":"arXiv","title":"A tiny Galactic dust cloud projected onto NGC 3269?"}],"curated":true}},{"created":"2014-10-31T00:00:00+00:00","links":{"bibtex":"https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/1325065?format=bibtex","latex-eu":"https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/1325065?format=latex-eu","latex-us":"https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/1325065?format=latex-us","json":"https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/1325065?format=json","json-expanded":"https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/1325065?format=json-expanded","cv":"https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/1325065?format=cv","citations":"https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/?q=refersto%3Arecid%3A1325065"},"updated":"2023-03-07T03:01:14.996673+00:00","id":"1325065","metadata":{"authors":[{"raw_affiliations":[{"value":"Department of Physics and ITCP, University of Crete, 71003 Heraklion, Greece"},{"value":"Foundation for Research and Technology - Hellas, IESL, Voutes, 7110 Heraklion, Greece"}],"full_name_unicode_normalized":"tassis, konstantinos","full_name":"Tassis, Konstantinos","record":{"$ref":"https://inspirehep.net/api/authors/1037950"},"affiliations":[{"record":{"$ref":"https://inspirehep.net/api/institutions/903969"},"value":"Crete U."},{"record":{"$ref":"https://inspirehep.net/api/institutions/912413"},"value":"IESL, Heraklion"}],"ids":[{"schema":"INSPIRE BAI","value":"K.Tassis.1"}],"last_name":"Tassis","signature_block":"TASk","first_name":"Konstantinos","uuid":"ec63109e-b3a1-46f1-bb8f-55d2eca35f26","recid":1037950},{"raw_affiliations":[{"value":"Department of